Node-local kubelet configuration written by kubeadm is not discarded anymore.
Previously, Tarook overwrote ``/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml`` with the content of the cluster-wide ``kubelet-config`` ConfigMap merged with the configured kubelet options.
This dropped settings which kubeadm determines per node,
most notably ``resolvConf`` on nodes running systemd-resolved
(`#909 <https://gitlab.com/alasca.cloud/tarook/tarook/-/work_items/909>`__).
On clusters created with kubeadm v1.35.9, v1.36.5, v1.37.1 or newer,
which do not store that value in the ConfigMap anymore,
this caused CoreDNS to crash loop.
Now kubeadm writes the file and applies the configured kubelet options of the node as a kubeadm patch,
also on ``kubeadm join`` and ``kubeadm upgrade``.
Nested options are merged into the values written by kubeadm instead of replacing them.
Patches from :ref:`configuration-options.yk8s.kubernetes.kubeadm.patches.kubeletconfiguration` are not discarded anymore either.
The workaround of setting ``resolvConf`` explicitly is not needed anymore.
